/* The 97k theme's login and character-scene system menu (SysMenuWin): the 0.97k ESC menu (its
   RenderErrorMessage() state 110), the same one the theme's world shows (generic_menu_dialog.rcss,
   kind system-menu). No box and no dimming: each button is Message_box (213x64 of it) squeezed to
   120x22, centred on the 640x480 screen (from 260), the first at 60 and each 30 below the last,
   its label white and centred 5 below its top. The login scene has Exit Game, Option and Close,
   the character scene Select Server too, as the 0.97k client had.

   The 0.97k drew a hovered button again over itself, additively, tinted (0.8, 0.6, 0.4); as in
   generic_menu_dialog.rcss, a part sepia then brightened stands in for it.

   #panel is the 0.97k screen's column of buttons: the screen is 640x480 dp centred in the window,
   as the theme's login box and server list place theirs (login.rcss), so the column's top is 60
   below the screen's (240 above the window's middle). */

@spritesheet sm97-btn-sheet { src: "../../../../Interface97/Message_box.jpg"; sm97-btn: 0px 0px 213px 64px; }

#backdrop { background-color: transparent; }

#panel {
	left: 50%;
	top: 50%;
	width: 120dp;
	height: auto;
	margin-left: -60dp;
	margin-top: -180dp;
	transform: none;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	color: #ffffff;
}
#panel .panel-middle, #panel .panel-cap-top, #panel .panel-cap-bottom { display: none; }

#panel .btn {
	display: block;
	position: static;
	width: 120dp;
	height: 22dp;
	line-height: 22dp;
	margin-bottom: 8dp;
	white-space: nowrap;
	decorator: image(sm97-btn fill);
}
#panel .btn:hover { decorator: image(sm97-btn fill); filter: sepia(0.6) brightness(1.5); }
#panel .btn:active { decorator: image(sm97-btn fill); image-color: rgb(200, 200, 200); }
#panel .btn.hidden { display: none; }
